# Scheduled jobs — Business Ops Tracker (R-6)
#
# Install on the server (phone SSH) with:
#   crontab deploy/crontab
# Verify with:
#   crontab -l
# and record the output in the go-live runbook (§2C). Cron runs with a
# minimal environment: the `cd` + compose file path below are load-bearing,
# and the jobs run INSIDE the running container (`docker compose exec`),
# so they see the container's environment (DATABASE_URL,
# MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL, etc.) as baked in at `docker compose up` time.
# If you change a secret, re-run `up -d` before relying on these jobs.
#
# Heartbeat / dead-man check: the JobHeartbeat mechanism (alert if a job
# has not run in > 36 h) is a separate workstream — until it lands, the
# check is manual: the logs below must show a fresh line after each
# scheduled time, and the Chairman reviews them (see runbook §2C).
#
# Times are server time (Asia/Yangon on the VPS).

# --- scheduled_alerts: missing-report reminders + document/batch expiry
# alerts. Daily 08:30. Idempotent (one notification per CEO per run,
# one alert per document per 7 days) — safe to re-run by hand.
# Log: ~/bot-alerts.log
30 8 * * * cd ~/business-ops-tracker && docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml exec -T app python -m src.jobs.scheduled_alerts >> ~/bot-alerts.log 2>&1

# --- audit_retention: delete sign-in/out rows older than 90 days, clear
# IPs older than 30 days; financial/account rows are KEPT as tamper
# evidence. Weekly, Sunday 03:00. MUST run as the schema-owner role:
# the runtime role (bot_app) deliberately cannot DELETE audit_logs (see
# deploy/db_roles.sql), so running this with the wrong URL fails with
# "permission denied" instead of silently doing nothing — that failure
# in ~/bot-audit-retention.log means MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL was not set
# when the container was started; re-run `up -d` with it set.
# Runs inside the app container, which already has
# MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL from the compose environment.
# Log: ~/bot-audit-retention.log
0 3 * * 0 cd ~/business-ops-tracker && docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml exec -T app python -m src.scripts.audit_retention >> ~/bot-audit-retention.log 2>&1

# --- log_scan: daily count of ERROR / journal-failure / lockout lines in
# the last 24 h of app logs. Daily 09:00. This is the minimum-viable
# monitoring until Sentry/a real alerting path exists: the Chairman
# reviews ~/bot-log-scan.log daily. A non-empty file means something
# needs the incident runbook. `|| true` because grep exits 1 when
# nothing matches, which cron would otherwise report as a job failure.
# Log: ~/bot-log-scan.log
0 9 * * * cd ~/business-ops-tracker && docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml logs --since 24h app 2>&1 | grep -iE 'ERROR|journal failed|lockout' >> ~/bot-log-scan.log 2>&1 || true

# --- backup: weekly pg_dump to separate storage (R-4). Weekly, Sunday
# 03:30. BACKUP_DIR must be off the app disk eventually (copy the dumps
# elsewhere); the script keeps 28 days of dumps. Runs on the host (not
# in the container) because it shells out to pg_dump / docker.
# Log: ~/bot-backup.log
30 3 * * 0 cd ~/business-ops-tracker && BACKUP_DIR=~/bot-backups ./scripts/backup.sh >> ~/bot-backup.log 2>&1
